# Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in. Read by post.py only - CI never sees
# any of this and must not: the cookie is what the account is.
# The fork is the patched TiktokAutoUploader checkout; see its own runbook for
# `cli.py login` and for tau-synergy.patch, without which post.py refuses.
TIKTOK_TAU_DIR=C:\Users\you\Desktop\Projects\tau
# The name `cli.py login -n` saved the cookie as. Its OWN account - sharing one
# with another channel is how both get flagged together.
TIKTOK_TAU_USER=circles
# Only if the fork's venv is not <TIKTOK_TAU_DIR>\.venv
# TIKTOK_TAU_PYTHON=
# Strongly recommended: without it the account posts from this machine's IP,
# shared with every other channel on it.
# TIKTOK_PROXY=http://LOGIN:PASSWORD@gw.example.com:10000
# The user agent the cookie logged in with. Unset means the fork invents one,
# and the upload does not look like the browser that signed in.
# TIKTOK_UA=
# Where the node signer looks for playwright's browsers. Needed whenever they
# are not under the default AppData path, which on Windows is the normal case:
# a Store python redirects AppData for its children, so the installer writes
# one directory and the signer reads another. The fork's own checkout usually
# holds them - without this the upload dies at "Failed to parse signature data".
# TIKTOK_TAU_BROWSERS=<TIKTOK_TAU_DIR>\ms-playwright
# Seconds before an upload is called hung. Default 1800.
# TIKTOK_TAU_TIMEOUT=
